    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f7d26fda8d3ba968cf66a6f91bf839131f3e32fdecbae3427515c9a95af1a770",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Expanding the inner coprime weight correlation opens the two-scale notation into four cutoff combinations. For each combination Lemma 9.1 gives a hard support law: it vanishes once the shared parameter i exceeds the smaller cutoff. Within support, Möbius reparametrization and Lemma 1.4 separate a multiplicative main expression from two errors arising from different summation ranges. The lemma controls this inner correlation only; the outer diagonal summation remains undone.",
