    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_01a4e68e08c9bca0ba3b1750f1ae8e949e983fb76587f5ef1e72a6a2c64b575f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source turns the two-cutoff divisor-sum coefficients into a mollified detector S whose family first moment retains the contribution a(1)=1, while the identity S=LM+I+J makes a zero of L force S to be represented by the separately controlled I and J terms. Comparing that forced representation with the first and second moments yields a positive nonvanishing population.",
