    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_416a0b48a84e7c5b5cb7f5821060bd4aef50ce5cbcc060a2322028c67dd6e3bf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At a fixed point, the argument needs the lower cutoff mainly through the coefficient gap a(1)=1 and a(n)=0 for 1<n<=Y, without fixing the later power scale. For uniform nonvanishing, the source deliberately chooses Y=q^(1/4); after Cauchy transports a character-specific zero to a common interval center, that same gap identifies S-1 as an n>Y tail whose weighted square sum decays with the interval index.",
