    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5a27d692417a8e7ca771776c623ca7ec11860e04c7b39ed5cb9b7b2abbe368c3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Residues of the analytic kernel replace its contour representation by controlled powers of the index ratio. After the I mean square is restricted to the multiplicative diagonal, gcd/lcm coordinates and squarefree Möbius support reorganize the resulting weight correlation into local arithmetic data; truncation and support errors are bounded before the surviving main term is evaluated through an Euler product constant.",
